# Scrollbars match container background

Any scrollable element must not expose a contrasting scrollbar track that reveals the layer underneath.

## Pattern

1. Add class `scroll-match-bg` to the scrolling element.
2. Set `--scroll-bg` on that same element (or a parent) to its solid background color.
3. Optionally set `--scroll-thumb` for a subtle thumb (default: semi-transparent white/dark mix).

```css
.my-panel {
  --scroll-bg: #0e1118;
  --scroll-thumb: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  background: var(--scroll-bg);
  overflow: auto;
}
```

```html
<div class="my-panel scroll-match-bg">...</div>
```

## Rules

- Prefer solid `background` on scroll containers; avoid transparent scroll areas over busy UI.
- Track color = `--scroll-bg` (same as container), not `transparent`.
- Apply to textareas with overflow, panel lists, overlay bodies, and nested todo/code blocks.

Utility lives in `src/styles.css` (`.scroll-match-bg`).
